macOS: PCRE2, which the sentence splitter builds as a project of its own, was not told the processor of the build, so the x86_64 engine build of a universal Mac build made an arm64 PCRE2 and lipo refused to join the two ("have the same architectures (arm64)"). CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES is now passed on, on Apple only.

--- a/3rd_party/ssplit-cpp/cmake/FindPCRE2.cmake
+++ b/3rd_party/ssplit-cpp/cmake/FindPCRE2.cmake
@@ -64,6 +64,11 @@
   endif(ANDROID)
 
 
+  # macOS: the processor this build is for (JeffOffice builds the engine once per processor and joins them with lipo; without it PCRE2 is built for the build computer's)
+  if(APPLE AND CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES)
+    LIST(APPEND PCRE2_CONFIGURE_OPTIONS -DCMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES=${CMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES})
+  endif()
+
   if(WIN32 AND NOT MSVC)
     # MinGW: ExternalProject would otherwise default to NMake
     LIST(APPEND PCRE2_CONFIGURE_OPTIONS -G ${CMAKE_GENERATOR} -DCMAKE_MAKE_PROGRAM=${CMAKE_MAKE_PROGRAM} -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=${CMAKE_C_COMPILER})
